Subject: [PATCH] css: system colours follow the claimed platform

CSS system colours such as Highlight, ButtonFace, GrayText and LinkText
come from the platform the profile claims, not from the machine the
browser runs on. A Windows profile gets the default Windows 10 or 11
theme in light mode and Chrome's dark defaults in dark mode, a macOS
profile gets the macOS selection colours, and a Linux profile gets
Chrome's plain defaults. Highlight is blended the way the claimed
platform blends it, so a light Windows profile reads rgb(0, 120, 215).
The profile fields theme.highlight_argb and theme.highlight_text_argb
are parsed and ignored.

diff --git a/ui/color/css_system_color_mixer.cc b/ui/color/css_system_color_mixer.cc
--- a/ui/color/css_system_color_mixer.cc
+++ b/ui/color/css_system_color_mixer.cc
